   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Lieutenant Donald R. Hill Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S6265",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6265-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-r, amd §343-k, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6265\n\nSPONSOR: RYAN C\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Lieutenant Donald R. Hill Memorial\nHighway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to designate a portion of the state highway\nsystem in Oswego, NY as the \"Lieutenant Donald R. Hill Memorial High-\nway.\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would amend the Highway Law by adding a new\nsection that designates a position of state route 104, between City Line\nRoad and Jim Shampine Drive in the City of Oswego, County of Oswego, to\nbe known as the \"Lieutenant Donald R. Hill Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSection 2 of this bill would amend the Highway Law by accepting a\nportion of the state highway designated as the \"Lake Ontario Wine\nTrail.\"\n\nSection 3 of this bill would provide parameters for the Commissioner of\nTransportation related to the installation and maintenance of adequate\nsignage of the designated memorial highway and require that the desig-\nnation shall be ceremonial in nature and the official name of such high-\nway shall not be changed.\n\nSection 4 of this bill provides that the effective date shall take\neffect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nLieutenant Donald R. Hill, born July bth, 1952, resided at 244 Munn St.\nin the City of Oswego and was 43 at the time that he was killed in the\nline of duty. Lt. Hill was appointed to the Oswego Police Department on\nSeptember 10th, 1975 and was planning on a near retirement, after serv-\ning more than 20 years with the department. On November llth, 1995,\nLieutenant Hill was one of two officers directing traffic for an over-\ntime detail on State Route 104 East when he was struck by a vehicle and\ndied from injuries sustained in the accident.\n\nLt. Hill was known for his cheerful, calm, even-mannered personality.\nLt. Hill was a well-respected husband, father, and police officer.  This\ndedication will serve not only to honor the life and legacy of Lt. Hill,\nbut to also serve as a reminder to motorists of the need to take caution\non our roadways. This bill would designate a portion of State Route 104\nbetween City Line Road and Jim Shampine Drive in the City of Oswego as\nthe \"Lieutenant Donald R. Hill Memorial Highway\"\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\nMinimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
